        "heading": "36 Countries. One Material. One Method.",
        "body": "<p>Since 2012, people in 36+ countries have built bamboo bicycles using BBC's methods. Three international workshop franchises — Munich (est. 2014), Amersfoort, Netherlands (est. 2019), and Toulouse, France (est. 2024) — run independent weekly programmes. In 2017, pupils at a school in The Hague built 7 bamboo bikes using our educational starter kit. In 2023, Kate Rawles cycled 8,288 miles from Colombia to Ushuaia on a bamboo bike built at our London workshop from UK-sourced materials.</p>",
